# 🎵 SyncWave

> **Real-time synchronized music listening — together, no matter where you are.**

SyncWave lets you and your friends listen to music in perfect sync. Create a room, invite others, and enjoy shared listening sessions with uploaded audio files or YouTube streams — all controlled with live playback, a queue, and in-session chat.

---

## ✨ Features

- 🔴 **Live Room System** — Create or join rooms with a 6-character code
- 🎧 **Synchronized Playback** — Every listener hears the same thing at the same moment
- 📁 **Audio File Upload** — Drag & drop MP3, WAV, FLAC, OGG, M4A (up to 50MB each)
- ▶️ **YouTube Streaming** — Paste any YouTube URL to add it to the queue
- 📋 **Shared Queue** — Add, reorder, and remove tracks collaboratively
- 🔒 **Permission System** — Hosts grant or revoke playback control per listener
- 💬 **Live Chat** — In-room messaging with unread badge notifications
- ⚡ **Real-time Sync** — Latency-compensated position syncing for new joiners
- 🌐 **WebSocket Powered** — Built on Socket.IO for low-latency communication

---

## 🖼️ Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| **Frontend** | React 18, Socket.IO Client, YouTube IFrame API |
| **Backend** | Node.js, Express, Socket.IO, Multer |
| **Real-time** | WebSocket (Socket.IO) |
| **Containerization** | Docker (multi-stage build) |

---

## 📁 Project Structure

```
syncwave/
├── client/                  # React frontend
│   ├── public/
│   │   └── index.html       # YouTube IFrame API script tag
│   └── src/
│       ├── App.js           # Main component (landing + room UI)
│       └── index.js         # React entry point
├── server/
│   ├── index.js             # Express + Socket.IO server
│   ├── uploads/             # Uploaded audio files (auto-created)
│   └── package.json
├── Dockerfile               # Multi-stage production build
└── README.md
```

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- **Node.js** 18 or higher
- **npm** 9 or higher
- **Docker** (optional, for containerized deployment)

---

### Local Development

#### 1. Start the Server

```bash
cd server
npm install
npm start
```

The server starts on **http://localhost:3001**

#### 2. Start the Client

Open a new terminal:

```bash
cd client
npm install
npm start
```

The React app starts on **http://localhost:3000**

> The client proxies API calls and WebSocket connections to the server automatically.

---

### Environment Variables

By default, the client connects to `http://localhost:3001`. To point to a different server, set:

```bash
REACT_APP_SERVER=https://your-server-url.com
```

---

## 🐳 Docker

Build and run the full application in a single container:

```bash
# Build the image
docker build -t syncwave .

# Run the container
docker run -p 3001:3001 syncwave
```

Then open **http://localhost:3001** in your browser.

The Dockerfile uses a multi-stage build:
1. **Stage 1** — Builds the React client
2. **Stage 2** — Sets up the Node.js server and copies the built client into it

---

## 🎮 How to Use

### Creating a Room

1. Enter your name on the landing page
2. Click **Create a Room**
3. Share the 6-character room code with friends (click it to copy)

### Joining a Room

1. Enter your name and the room code
2. Click **Join**

### Adding Music

If you have playback control (host or granted permission):

- **Upload Tab** — Drag & drop audio files or click to browse
- **YouTube Tab** — Paste a YouTube URL and click Add

### Host Controls

- Click the 🔓/🔒 icon next to any listener to grant or revoke their playback control
- The host always retains control
- If the host leaves, the room is dissolved

---

## 🔌 API Reference

### REST Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| `POST` | `/upload` | Upload an audio file (multipart/form-data, field: `audio`) |
| `GET` | `/room/:roomId` | Get current room state (members, queue, playback state) |

### Socket.IO Events

#### Client → Server

| Event | Payload | Description |
|-------|---------|-------------|
| `create_room` | `{ name }` | Create a new room |
| `join_room` | `{ roomId, name }` | Join an existing room |
| `play_pause` | `{ roomId, playing, position }` | Toggle playback |
| `seek` | `{ roomId, position }` | Seek to position (seconds) |
| `add_to_queue` | `{ roomId, track }` | Add an uploaded track |
| `stream_track` | `{ roomId, youtubeId, title, thumbnail }` | Add a YouTube track |
| `next_track` | `{ roomId }` | Skip to next track |
| `prev_track` | `{ roomId }` | Go to previous track |
| `remove_from_queue` | `{ roomId, trackId }` | Remove a track from queue |
| `toggle_permission` | `{ roomId, memberId }` | Grant/revoke listener control (host only) |
| `chat_message` | `{ roomId, text }` | Send a chat message |

#### Server → Client

| Event | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `room_created` | Emitted to host after room creation |
| `room_joined` | Emitted to joiner with current room state |
| `sync_state` | Playback sync broadcast to all room members |
| `queue_updated` | Broadcast when queue or track changes |
| `members_updated` | Broadcast when a member joins/leaves/permission changes |
| `permission_changed` | Emitted to the affected member |
| `chat_message` | Broadcast chat message to all members |
| `room_dissolved` | Emitted when the host disconnects |
| `user_joined` / `user_left` | Notification events for room activity |

---

## 🏗️ Architecture Notes

- **Room state** is stored in-memory on the server. Restarting the server clears all rooms.
- **Playback sync** accounts for network latency: the server timestamps every sync event and the client compensates by adding elapsed time when calculating the correct seek position.
- **YouTube audio** uses the hidden YouTube IFrame Player API — all listeners load the same video client-side, controlled by sync events.
- **File uploads** are stored in `server/uploads/` and served as static files. Files persist until the server restarts (or the directory is cleared).

---

## ⚠️ Known Limitations

- Room state is **not persisted** — server restarts clear all rooms and queues
- Uploaded files are **not cleaned up** automatically
- YouTube playback sync may vary slightly due to YouTube's buffering behavior
- No authentication — anyone with a room code can join

---

## 🛠️ Development Tips

- Use `nodemon` for hot-reloading the server during development:
  ```bash
  cd server
  npm install -D nodemon
  npx nodemon index.js
  ```
- The client uses `react-scripts` (Create React App), so standard CRA tooling applies
- Socket events can be debugged in the browser console — Socket.IO logs connection details

